<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore and Brunei sign air services agreement.</title>
<headline>Singapore and Brunei sign air services agreement.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore and Brunei signed an air services agreement in Singapore on Saturday, the Civil Aviation Authority of Singapore said in a statement.</p>
<p>The agreement puts in place an open skies arrangement between the two countries allowing the carriers of both countries to respond more effectively to market forces, the statement said.</p>
<p>Currently, Singapore Airlines flies seven times a week to Brunei while Royal Brunei Airlines operates 17 services to Singapore.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65) 870-3080</p>
</text>
